course: dictionary
lesson: 275
title: Ambush: the surprise attack
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: An ambush is a surprise attack. People or animals hide and wait, then strike when their target comes close. «Cats are ambush hunters: they wait very still for a long time, creep close, and pounce in one short burst.» The waiting and hiding are the clues that this is an ambush.
explain: As a verb, to ambush someone means to hide and then attack them by surprise. «Lionesses hunt together, some driving prey towards others hiding in ambush.» Here some lionesses hide, and the prey does not see them coming.
explain: Look for clue words around ambush: hiding, waiting, still, creep, pounce, surprise. Then check by swapping in your meaning. Does «they waited hidden, then attacked by surprise» still make sense? If yes, you have found the right meaning.
explain: Ambush also has a jokey, informal use. «Mum ambushed me with questions about homework» does not mean she attacked you. It means she surprised you with difficult questions. The context tells you which meaning the writer wants.
fact: An ambush is a surprise attack made by people or animals who have been hiding and waiting.
fact: «Crocodiles» lie still like logs at the water's edge and ambush animals that come to drink.
fact: To lie in ambush means to wait hidden, ready to attack.
fact: The verb forms are ambush, ambushes, ambushed and ambushing: «Cats ambushed the mouse» uses the past tense.
fact: Informal use: to ambush someone can mean to surprise them with difficult questions or a sudden request.
exercise: «Crocodiles ... lie still like logs at the water's edge and ambush animals that come to drink.» What does ambush mean here? | *A surprise attack from hiding | Making a loud noise | Swimming fast to race the animals | Sleeping in the sun
exercise: «Cats are ambush hunters.» What kind of hunters are cats in this sentence? | *Hunters that wait hidden and strike by surprise | Hunters that chase their prey for miles | Hunters that only eat plants | Hunters that always hunt in a group
exercise: «Mum ambushed me with questions about homework.» What does ambushed mean in this jokey sense? | She sent me a text message | She attacked me with a cushion | She hid and waited in the garden | *She surprised me with difficult questions
test: «Lionesses hunt together, some driving prey towards others hiding in ambush.» Who is hiding in ambush? | *Other lionesses | The keepers at the zoo | The buffalo | The prey alone
test: Which phrase means to wait hidden, ready to attack? | Run for home | Sing loudly | *Lie in ambush | Walk away quietly
exam: Which sentence uses ambush in the informal sense? | The cat crept close and pounced | The lion lay in ambush behind the rock | The crocodile waited still at the water's edge | *Grandma ambushed me with a sudden question about my spelling test
